     6	
     7	   Each integer value has exactly one carrier per host:
     8	
     9	   | Host | Native carrier                      | Big carrier          |
    10	   |------|-------------------------------------|----------------------|
    11	   | JVM  | `long`, signed 64-bit               | `clojure.lang.BigInt`|
    12	   | JS   | `Number`, within +/-(2^53 - 1)      | host `BigInt`        |
    13	   | Dart | `int`, signed 64-bit                | `BigInt`             |
    14	
    15	   `promote` turns any exact-integer carrier into the host big integer
    16	   the operations below take (`java.math.BigInteger` on the JVM, which
    17	   never leaves this namespace and `yin.vm.integer`); `demote` turns a
    18	   result back into its canonical carrier. JavaScript holds +/-2^53 as a
    19	   `BigInt`, never as an unsafe `Number`, and a JavaScript `-0` is
    20	   floating-point content, not an integer, as `dao.jing.cbor` classifies
    21	   it.
    22	
    23	   This namespace depends on nothing: it does not reach into
    24	   `dao.jing.cbor`'s private big-integer helpers, so Jing stays a passive
    25	   codec. Every reader conditional names `:cljd` first, because the
    26	   ClojureDart build also reads `:clj`."
